---
// Hand-authored inline SVG: two boundaries drawn over roughly the same place,
// and the different answers they produce for the Loop and for Gary, Indiana.
// Inline for the same reasons as RegionGraphNYC.astro — see that file's header.
//
// Nodes and edges transcribed from the shipped seed data:
//   chicago          parents = ["cook-county"]                    regions_us.toml
//   cook-county      parents = ["chicago-metro", "rta-service-area"]
//   rta-service-area parents = ["il"]                             regions_us_multistate.toml
//   chicago-metro    parents = ["chicagoland"]                    regions_us_msas.toml
//   gary             parents = ["lake-county-in"]                 regions_us.toml
//   lake-county-in   parents = ["chicago-metro", "in"]            regions_us.toml
//   chicagoland / il / in  parents = []
//
// The chicagoland node is named "Chicagoland (IL/IN/WI)" in the seed; the label
// here is trimmed to "Chicagoland" because the post only ever discusses Illinois
// and Indiana, and no WI edge exists for a reader to trace. Node names are a
// display choice; edges are not — those stay verbatim.
//
// Two things deliberately absent. chicago-metro's rollup_states = ["il", "in"]
// is browse-only and never walked, so no edge. The five collar counties
// (DuPage, Kane, Lake-IL, McHenry, Will) are all in the shipped seed with the
// same parents as cook-county, but drawing five identical nodes would add
// nothing the "Cook + 5 collar" subtitle doesn't already say.
//
// Styles live in global.css (.post-diagram) per the one-stylesheet rule.
---

<figure class="post-figure post-diagram">
  <svg
    viewBox="0 0 700 600"
    role="img"
    aria-labelledby="dg-chi-title dg-chi-desc"
    class="dg"
  >
    <title id="dg-chi-title">
      The Chicago metro area and the RTA service area as separate regions
    </title>
    <desc id="dg-chi-desc">
      A directed graph with two paths. From Chicago, the lookup climbs through
      Cook County, which has two parents: the Chicago Metro area, and the RTA
      Service Area, whose parent is Illinois. So a search from the Loop reaches
      both the metro and the transit district. From Gary, Indiana, the lookup
      climbs through Lake County, Indiana, whose parents are the Chicago Metro
      area and the state of Indiana. Gary therefore reaches the metro but never
      the RTA and never Illinois, because the metro has no edge to either state.
      Both paths converge on Chicago Metro and then Chicagoland.
    </desc>

    <defs>
      <marker
        id="dg-chi-arrow"
        viewBox="0 0 10 10"
        refX="9"
        refY="5"
        markerWidth="6"
        markerHeight="6"
        orient="auto-start-reverse"
      >
        <path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z" class="dg-arrowhead" />
      </marker>
      <marker
        id="dg-chi-arrow-a"
        viewBox="0 0 10 10"
        refX="9"
        refY="5"
        markerWidth="6"
        markerHeight="6"
        orient="auto-start-reverse"
      >
        <path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z" class="dg-arrowhead dg-arrowhead--a" />
      </marker>
    </defs>

    {/* ---- edges ---- */}
    <g class="dg-edges" fill="none">
      {/* the Loop's walk — and, above the merge, the spine both walks share */}
      <g marker-end="url(#dg-chi-arrow-a)">
        <path class="dg-edge dg-edge--a" d="M305 482 V 436" />
        <path class="dg-edge dg-edge--a" d="M305 394 V 180 H 355 V 154" />
        <path class="dg-edge dg-edge--a" d="M230 412 H 90 V 350" />
        <path class="dg-edge dg-edge--a" d="M90 296 V 252" />
        <path class="dg-edge dg-edge--a" d="M355 112 V 64" />
      </g>
      {/* Gary's walk — joins the spine at the metro and never touches the left side */}
      <g marker-end="url(#dg-chi-arrow)">
        <path class="dg-edge" d="M530 482 V 436" />
        <path class="dg-edge" d="M530 394 V 180 H 355 V 154" />
        <path class="dg-edge" d="M610 412 H 625 V 252" />
      </g>
    </g>

    {/* ---- nodes ---- */}
    <g class="dg-group">
      <rect x="250" y="22" width="210" height="36" class="dg-node" />
      <text x="355" y="45" class="dg-label">Chicagoland</text>
    </g>

    <g class="dg-group">
      <rect x="270" y="112" width="170" height="36" class="dg-node" />
      <text x="355" y="135" class="dg-label">Chicago Metro</text>
    </g>

    <g class="dg-group">
      <rect x="20" y="216" width="140" height="36" class="dg-node" />
      <text x="90" y="239" class="dg-label">Illinois</text>
    </g>

    <g class="dg-group">
      <rect x="560" y="216" width="130" height="36" class="dg-node" />
      <text x="625" y="239" class="dg-label">Indiana</text>
    </g>

    <g class="dg-group">
      <rect x="13" y="296" width="154" height="48" class="dg-node" />
      <text x="90" y="316" class="dg-label">RTA Service Area</text>
      <text x="90" y="333" class="dg-sub">Cook + 5 collar counties</text>
    </g>

    <g class="dg-group">
      <rect x="230" y="394" width="150" height="36" class="dg-node" />
      <text x="305" y="417" class="dg-label">Cook County</text>
    </g>

    <g class="dg-group">
      <rect x="450" y="394" width="160" height="36" class="dg-node" />
      <text x="530" y="417" class="dg-label">Lake County, IN</text>
    </g>

    <g class="dg-group">
      <rect x="225" y="482" width="160" height="36" class="dg-node" />
      <text x="305" y="505" class="dg-label">Chicago — the Loop</text>
    </g>
    <text x="305" y="541" class="dg-call">60601 anchors here</text>

    <g class="dg-group">
      <rect x="455" y="482" width="150" height="36" class="dg-node" />
      <text x="530" y="505" class="dg-label">Gary, Indiana</text>
    </g>
    <text x="530" y="541" class="dg-call">46402 anchors here</text>

    {/* ---- legend ---- */}
    <g class="dg-legend">
      <path class="dg-edge dg-edge--a" d="M20 578 H 56" fill="none" />
      <text x="64" y="582" class="dg-note dg-note--start">lookup from 60601 (the Loop)</text>
      <path class="dg-edge" d="M250 578 H 286" fill="none" />
      <text x="294" y="582" class="dg-note dg-note--start">lookup from 46402 (Gary, IN)</text>
    </g>
  </svg>

  <figcaption>
    Two shapes over roughly the same place. The metro crosses into Indiana; the
    RTA stops at the Illinois line. Because Chicago Metro has no edge to either
    state, Gary picks up the metro and Indiana but never the RTA and never
    Illinois — no special-casing required, just the graph.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
